// ============================================================================
// Harmonic PRZ Matrix Scanner — Gartley / Bat / Butterfly / Crab
// TradingView Pine Script v6 STRATEGY (not a plain indicator)
//
// Reference implementation for PRD.md §1.6, §3, §5–§7, §11 (Phase 1).
// Every ratio, invalidation, stop and target below is taken verbatim from the
// PRD's corrected §3.2 table — NOT from the original design brief, which
// contained the bugs this script deliberately avoids:
//   - no BC projection / AB=CD checks              -> added here (§3.2)
//   - Butterfly/Crab stop = own PRZ edge (0 buffer) -> stopR extends past it
//   - "1.130 XA" stop applied to all patterns        -> stop ratio is per-pattern
//   - targets measured off the CD leg                -> targets are on the AD leg
//   - blind limit order at D                         -> requires an engulfing
//                                                        confirmation inside the
//                                                        zone before any entry
//
// WHY A strategy() AND NOT AN indicator()
//   A strategy() is what makes historical validation real rather than asserted:
//   TradingView's own Strategy Tester replays this script's strategy.entry /
//   strategy.exit calls across every historical bar on whatever chart you load
//   it onto, and reports win rate, profit factor, drawdown and a full trade
//   list computed from THIS code, not from a claim in a document.
//
// HOW TO HISTORICALLY VALIDATE THIS SCRIPT (PRD §11.5)
//   1. Non-repainting check: apply to a liquid chart (e.g. BTCUSDT, 1H), open
//      Bar Replay, step forward. A drawn pattern polygon/PRZ box must NEVER
//      disappear or move on a later bar — only ever turn stale/invalidated.
//      This is guaranteed structurally here: ta.pivothigh/pivotlow only ever
//      return a value `pivotDepth` bars AFTER the pivot bar, once confirmed.
//   2. Case-study reproduction: load XAG/USD on a daily chart around the
//      corrected PRD §10.1 dates. The script's plotted B should print near
//      61.97 (78.6% of XA), and the PRZ band near 66.10 (1.270 XA) — NOT the
//      source brief's incorrect 61.10 / 64.88-65.21. See the worked check at
//      the bottom of this file.
//   3. Strategy Tester: open the "Strategy Tester" tab -> Performance Summary
//      for net profit / win rate / profit factor, and List of Trades to
//      cross-check individual fills against the on-chart PRZ/stop/TP levels.
//      Commission (0.05%) and slippage (2 ticks) are set as fixed defaults in
//      the strategy() declaration below — override them from the chart's
//      "Properties" tab -> "Commission and slippage" to match your venue
//      before drawing ANY conclusion from the numbers (PRD §7.2, §11.5 step 3).
//   4. Gate verification: in the trade list, confirm no trade's stop sits
//      inside the PRZ it entered from, and every trade's realized R:R to TP2
//      is >= rrMin. A violation is a script defect, not a market outcome.
//
// SCOPE (PRD §1.6, §11 Phase 1): Gartley, Bat, Butterfly, Crab. One symbol,
// one timeframe, per chart — this is a scanner for the chart it's applied to,
// not the multi-symbol watchlist scanner or the manual-plotting mode from the
// PRD (§5.3, §8) — Pine cannot provide either; see §1.6's disposition table.
// Shark (5-point O-X-A-B-C, §3.3) is Phase 2 and not implemented here.
//
// TOLERANCE NOTE (PRD §1.6 "Tolerance implementation note"): tolPct below is
// applied directly in ratio space to every constraint window (B, C, BC-proj,
// AB=CD, D) for implementation simplicity — the common convention in public
// Pine harmonic scripts. The PRZ envelope itself IS computed the spec-faithful
// way: three contributor prices, then a single price-width tolerance band
// (tolPct% of |A-X|) around their min/max (§6.2).
// ============================================================================

//@version=6
// Commission/slippage are fixed defaults here rather than script inputs — the
// strategy() declaration statement must be the first statement in the script,
// so it cannot reference input.*() variables declared elsewhere, and inlining
// input.*() calls as its own argument values is unreliable across Pine Editor
// versions. Override both from the chart's "Properties" tab -> "Commission
// and slippage" instead (PRD §7.2, §11.5 step 3 — do this before drawing ANY
// conclusion from the Strategy Tester; these defaults are deliberately non-zero
// so a fresh load isn't silently flattered, but they are still only a guess).
strategy("Harmonic PRZ Matrix — Gartley/Bat/Butterfly/Crab",
    shorttitle = "Harmonic PRZ",
    overlay = true,
    initial_capital = 10000,
    default_qty_type = strategy.fixed,
    default_qty_value = 1,
    pyramiding = 0,
    calc_on_every_tick = false,
    process_orders_on_close = true,
    commission_type = strategy.commission.percent,
    commission_value = 0.05,
    slippage = 2,
    max_lines_count = 300, max_boxes_count = 300, max_labels_count = 300)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Inputs ---
grpDet = "Detection (§5)"
pivotDepth = input.int(5, "Pivot confirmation depth (bars each side)", minval = 2, group = grpDet, tooltip = "A pivot only becomes visible pivotDepth bars after it forms — this is what makes detection non-repainting (§5.2 D1/D2).")
maxPivots  = input.int(60, "Max stored zig-zag points", minval = 12, group = grpDet)
showCandidates = input.bool(true, "Show diagnostic dot on any partial B/C match", group = grpDet, tooltip = "A full trade requires B, C, the PRZ, an engulfing confirmation AND the R:R gate to all pass on one structure — genuinely rare. This dot fires on the much weaker condition of just B and C matching some pattern's window, so you can see the scanner is alive between full setups.")

grpPat = "Patterns (§3.2)"
useGartley   = input.bool(true, "Gartley",   group = grpPat)
useBat       = input.bool(true, "Bat",       group = grpPat)
useButterfly = input.bool(true, "Butterfly", group = grpPat)
useCrab      = input.bool(true, "Crab",      group = grpPat)

grpRisk = "Tolerance & Risk (§2.4, §7)"
tolPct        = input.float(2.0, "Ratio tolerance (%, ratio-space — see file header)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)
rrMin         = input.float(2.0, "Minimum R:R to TP2 (§7.6 gate)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)
stopBufA      = input.float(0.05, "Extra stop buffer, in units of the §3.2 D-ratio (added to stopR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpRisk)
requireConfirm = input.bool(true, "Require engulfing confirmation inside the PRZ before entry (§7.4)", group = grpRisk)
riskPct       = input.float(1.0, "Risk % of equity per trade (§7.5)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- Types ---
type Pivot
    float price
    int   idx
    bool  isHigh

type PatternDef
    string name
    float  bLo
    float  bHi
    float  cLo
    float  cHi
    float  bcLo
    float  bcHi
    float  cdLo
    float  cdHi
    float  dLo
    float  dHi
    float  invalidR
    float  stopR
    color  col

// ------------------------------------------------------------ Persisted ---
// Declared before the helpers below, because a Pine function reading a global
// var must see it declared earlier in the script — Pine does not hoist.
var Pivot[]      zz       = array.new<Pivot>()
var PatternDef[] defs     = array.new<PatternDef>()
var int[]        lastSigC = array.new<int>()

// -------------------------------------------------------------- Helpers ---
inWindow(float val, float lo, float hi, float tol) =>
    val >= lo - tol and val <= hi + tol

// Confirmed, non-repainting zig-zag: only ever appends/replaces using
// ta.pivothigh/pivotlow output, which itself only resolves pivotDepth bars
// after the fact (§5.2 D1). Same-direction pivots collapse to the more
// extreme one; alternating pivots append, keeping X-A-B-C-D strictly
// alternating (§3.1 S1).
addPivot(float price, int idx, bool isHigh) =>
    n = array.size(zz)
    if n == 0
        array.push(zz, Pivot.new(price, idx, isHigh))
    else
        last = array.get(zz, n - 1)
        if last.isHigh == isHigh
            if (isHigh and price > last.price) or (not isHigh and price < last.price)
                array.set(zz, n - 1, Pivot.new(price, idx, isHigh))
        else
            array.push(zz, Pivot.new(price, idx, isHigh))
    if array.size(zz) > maxPivots
        array.shift(zz)

if barstate.isfirst
    if useGartley
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Gartley",   0.618, 0.618, 0.382, 0.886, 1.130, 1.618, 1.000, 1.000, 0.786, 0.786, 1.000, 1.050, color.new(color.blue, 0)))
    if useBat
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Bat",       0.382, 0.500, 0.382, 0.886, 1.618, 2.618, 1.270, 1.618, 0.886, 0.886, 1.000, 1.050, color.new(color.purple, 0)))
    if useButterfly
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Butterfly", 0.786, 0.786, 0.382, 0.886, 1.618, 2.240, 1.270, 1.618, 1.270, 1.618, 1.618, 1.750, color.new(color.orange, 0)))
    if useCrab
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Crab",      0.382, 0.618, 0.382, 0.886, 2.240, 3.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.902, color.new(color.red, 0)))
    for i = 0 to array.size(defs) - 1
        array.push(lastSigC, -1)

// ---------------------------------------------------------- Pivot feed  ---
ph = ta.pivothigh(pivotDepth, pivotDepth)
pl = ta.pivotlow(pivotDepth, pivotDepth)

if not na(ph)
    addPivot(ph, bar_index - pivotDepth, true)
if not na(pl)
    addPivot(pl, bar_index - pivotDepth, false)

// alertcondition/plotchar need plain series computed unconditionally every bar
var bool przActiveThisBar = false
var bool anyShapeOkThisBar = false
przActiveThisBar := false
anyShapeOkThisBar := false

// --------------------------------------------------- Candidate scanning ---
if array.size(zz) >= 4 and array.size(defs) > 0
    n = array.size(zz)
    X = array.get(zz, n - 4)
    A = array.get(zz, n - 3)
    B = array.get(zz, n - 2)
    C = array.get(zz, n - 1)

    xaLeg = A.price - X.price          // §2.1 P(A,X,r) = A + r*(X-A); sign of this leg carries direction
    abLeg = A.price - B.price
    bcLeg = C.price - B.price

    if xaLeg != 0 and abLeg != 0 and bcLeg != 0
        isBullish  = xaLeg > 0          // A>X: XA rises -> D projects down -> long at D (§2.3)
        dTestPrice = isBullish ? low : high

        // Only B and C are gated here (§2.2): both are fixed once C confirms and don't
        // depend on the still-forming D. BC-projection, AB=CD and the D-of-XA ratio are
        // NOT re-tested against dTestPrice here — instead the PRZ envelope below converts
        // each of their ratio windows directly into contributor PRICES (§6.1/§6.2), and
        // membership in the resulting union interval is what gates D. That is the
        // spec-faithful PRZ definition: a convergence band, not three independent checks
        // that all have to pass on the same live D estimate.
        bRatio = abLeg / xaLeg                              // §2.2 B retracement of XA
        cRatio = (C.price - B.price) / abLeg                // §2.2 C retracement of AB

        validSide = bRatio > 0 and cRatio > 0

        for i = 0 to array.size(defs) - 1
            pd = array.get(defs, i)

            shapeOk = validSide and inWindow(bRatio, pd.bLo, pd.bHi, tolPct / 100) and inWindow(cRatio, pd.cLo, pd.cHi, tolPct / 100)
            if shapeOk
                anyShapeOkThisBar := true

            if shapeOk
                // §6.1/§6.2 — PRZ envelope from three contributors, spec-faithful price tolerance
                pXAlo = A.price + pd.dLo * (X.price - A.price)
                pXAhi = A.price + pd.dHi * (X.price - A.price)
                pBClo = C.price - pd.bcLo * bcLeg
                pBChi = C.price - pd.bcHi * bcLeg
                pCDlo = C.price - pd.cdLo * abLeg
                pCDhi = C.price - pd.cdHi * abLeg
                tolPrice = (tolPct / 100) * math.abs(xaLeg)

                envLo = math.min(math.min(math.min(pXAlo, pXAhi), math.min(pBClo, pBChi)), math.min(pCDlo, pCDhi)) - tolPrice
                envHi = math.max(math.max(math.max(pXAlo, pXAhi), math.max(pBClo, pBChi)), math.max(pCDlo, pCDhi)) + tolPrice

                invalidPrice = A.price + pd.invalidR * (X.price - A.price)
                invalidBreached = isBullish ? dTestPrice < invalidPrice : dTestPrice > invalidPrice

                inZone = dTestPrice >= math.min(envLo, envHi) and dTestPrice <= math.max(envLo, envHi)

                if inZone and not invalidBreached
                    przActiveThisBar := true
                    box.new(C.idx, math.max(envLo, envHi), bar_index, math.min(envLo, envHi), xloc = xloc.bar_index, bgcolor = color.new(pd.col, 65), border_color = color.new(pd.col, 15), border_width = 2)

                    bullEngulf = close > open and close[1] < open[1] and close >= open[1] and open <= close[1]
                    bearEngulf = close < open and close[1] > open[1] and close <= open[1] and open >= close[1]
                    confirmed = not requireConfirm or (isBullish ? bullEngulf : bearEngulf)

                    if confirmed and array.get(lastSigC, i) != C.idx
                        // §7.1 — stop ratio is per-pattern (from pd.stopR), never per trading-style
                        stopPrice = A.price + (pd.stopR + stopBufA) * (X.price - A.price)
                        entryPrice = dTestPrice
                        adLeg = A.price - entryPrice
                        tp1 = entryPrice + 0.382 * adLeg     // §7.3 — targets on the AD leg, not CD
                        tp2 = entryPrice + 0.618 * adLeg
                        risk = math.abs(entryPrice - stopPrice)
                        rr2 = risk > 0 ? math.abs(tp2 - entryPrice) / risk : 0.0

                        if risk > 0 and rr2 >= rrMin        // §7.6 — hard R:R gate
                            array.set(lastSigC, i, C.idx)
                            qty = (strategy.equity * riskPct / 100) / risk
                            entryId = pd.name + "_" + str.tostring(C.idx)

                            if isBullish
                                strategy.entry(entryId, strategy.long, qty = qty)
                            else
                                strategy.entry(entryId, strategy.short, qty = qty)
                            strategy.exit(entryId + "_x1", from_entry = entryId, stop = stopPrice, limit = tp1, qty_percent = 50)
                            strategy.exit(entryId + "_x2", from_entry = entryId, stop = stopPrice, limit = tp2, qty_percent = 50)

                            line.new(X.idx, X.price, A.idx, A.price, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)
                            line.new(A.idx, A.price, B.idx, B.price, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)
                            line.new(B.idx, B.price, C.idx, C.price, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)
                            line.new(C.idx, C.price, bar_index, entryPrice, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)

                            dirTxt = isBullish ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
                            lbl = pd.name + " " + dirTxt + "  R:R " + str.tostring(rr2, "#.##")
                            label.new(bar_index, entryPrice, text = lbl, xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = isBullish ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = pd.col, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

                            alert(pd.name + " " + dirTxt + " confirmed — entry " + str.tostring(entryPrice) + " stop " + str.tostring(stopPrice) + " TP2 " + str.tostring(tp2) + " R:R " + str.tostring(rr2, "#.##"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

alertcondition(przActiveThisBar, title = "PRZ Active", message = "Price entered a harmonic PRZ zone on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")

// Diagnostic only — NOT a trade signal. Fires on the much weaker condition of B
// and C alone matching some enabled pattern's window (§2.2), which happens far
// more often than a full PRZ entry + confirmation + R:R pass. If this dot never
// appears either, no candidate shape is forming at all on this symbol/timeframe/
// tolerance — try a wider tolPct, a smaller pivotDepth, or a choppier symbol.
plotchar(showCandidates and anyShapeOkThisBar ? high : na, title = "Candidate B/C match (diagnostic, not a signal)", char = "•", location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.gray, 40), size = size.tiny)

// ============================================================================
// WORKED CHECKS — PRD §10, reproduced here so the arithmetic above is
// auditable by hand against the same numbers the PRD verified in Python.
//
// Case Study 1 (corrected) — XAG/USD Bearish Butterfly
//   X=63.80  A=55.27  (xaLeg = A-X = -8.53, isBullish = false)
//   B should print near 61.97 -> bRatio = (A-B)/xaLeg = (55.27-61.97)/-8.53 = 0.786  [target 0.786]
//   D-of-XA envelope center (1.270) -> A + 1.270*(X-A) = 55.27 + 1.270*8.53 = 66.10
//   stop = A + 1.750*(X-A) = 55.27 + 1.750*8.53 = 70.19  (beyond the 1.618 far edge, non-zero gap)
//
// Case Study 2 (replacement) — BTC/USDT Bullish Bat
//   X=53500  A=71980  (xaLeg = A-X = 18480, isBullish = true)
//   D-of-XA at 0.886 -> A + 0.886*(X-A) = 71980 + 0.886*(53500-71980) = 55,607  [matches §10.2]
//   stop = A + 1.050*(X-A) = 71980 + 1.050*(-18480) = 52,576  (below X, non-zero gap to invalidation)
// ============================================================================
